    "https://www.gu.se/en/work-at-the-university-of-gothenburg/how-to-apply-for-a-position": {
      "title": "How to apply for a position",
      "description": "How to apply for a position | University of Gothenburg Close Go straight to Main content Enter Go straight to Menu Enter Go straight to Search function Enter Go straight to Footer Enter Go straight to Contact the university Enter Go straight to About the website Enter Notice: Some functionality may be limited if JavaScript is disabled, please enable JavaScript for a better experience. Menu Contact Svenska English Close main menu University of Gothenburg Study Submenu for Study Programs and courses Submenu for Programs and courses Master's programs Bachelor's programs Double and joint degrees Sustainability labelled programs Find courses Find syllabus and reading list Study Swedish University studies in Sweden Study guidance Apply Submenu for Apply Apply for Master's program Apply for Bachelor's program Apply for courses Key dates admission 2026 Tuition fees Submenu for Tuition fees Tuition fees terms and conditions Scholarships for fee-paying students Submenu for Scholarships for fee-paying students Axel Adler Scholarship Scholarships for students at the School of Business, Economics and Law SI Scholarship Women in STEM Deferring your studies Meet the University Campus and student life Submenu for Campus and student life Academic calendar Introduction days Campus and facilities International opportunities Student Services and Support Study with a disability Student testimonials Prepare for your arrival Submenu for Prepare for your arrival Before you arrive Residence permits and visa Living costs Getting started Incoming exchange student Submenu for Incoming exchange student Apply for exchange studies Find courses for exchange students Apply for exchange courses Exchange courses taught in Swedish Contact my international coordinator After your studies Submenu for After your studies Different types of degrees Submenu for Different types of degrees Main fields of study Qualifications in the Fine, Applied and Performing Arts Working in Sweden Alumni Research Submenu for Research Research areas Submenu for Research areas Sustainability and the environment Health and medicine Culture and languages Science and IT Society and economics Education and learning Find research Excellent research Strategic research areas Research ethics Submenu for Research ethics Animal testing at the University Research infrastructure Doctoral studies Submenu for Doctoral studies About doctoral education Apply to doctoral studies Doctoral courses Before you arrive Getting started Collaboration and innovation Submenu for Collaboration and innovation Networks, partners and collaborations Submenu for Networks, partners and collaborations EUTOPIA The SDG 8 Initiative Innovation Collaborate with us Centres of expertise and research Events and venues About the University Submenu for About the University Contact Submenu for Contact Servicecenter Work at the University Submenu for Work at the University Gothenburg Global Scholars Initiative Vacancies Employment benefits How to apply for a position Before you arrive Getting started Organisation Submenu for Organisation The University Board Facts and figures Policy, rules and plans Vision and values Submenu for Vision and values Vision 2021-2030: A University for the World Sustainable development Submenu for Sustainable development Sustainability results 2025 We build the future citycampus Quality assurance in education and research Application for the HR Excellence in Research Award Find organisation Find staff Ranking and recognitions Ceremonies and traditions Submenu for Ceremonies and traditions New doctors: About your conferment Honorary doctors, promotors and frequently asked questions Inauguration of New Professors Widening access and participation History of the University of Gothenburg About Gothenburg News and events Submenu for News and events Find news Find events Press office Incident in the Canvas learning platform The University in a troubled world University of Gothenburg Contact Svenska English Search Menu Search Search Search Find staff Find courses Find research Find news Find organisation Find event Breadcrumb Home Work at the University of Gothenburg How to apply for a position Page content Step 1. Application Step 2. Selection Step 3. Offer and employment Collective agreement and union representatives FAQ Related content Page content Step 1. Application Step 2. Selection Step 3. Offer and employment Collective agreement and union representatives FAQ Related content How to apply for a position Do you want to work at the University of Gothenburg? Our checklist helps you, both before, during, and after you have applied for a position. Step 1. Application To apply for a position at the University of Gothenburg, you must register an account in our recruitment system. It is your responsibility to ensure that your application is complete according with the advertisement and that you submit it no later than 23:59 on the final application deadline. Find a job On the vacancies page , you can find our job listings. Once you have found a position you are interested in, you will need to register or log in to your account . You can do this by clicking the Apply button in the job announcement.. Answer Questions and Attach Documents After logging in, you will be directed to the application form for the position you wish to apply for. Be sure to answer mandatory questions and attach required documents. You can save your application and continue later within the application period. Register and Submit Your Application To submit your application, you first need to consent to the registration and processing of your personal data for recruitment purposes. You can edit your application until the end of the application period; thereafter, it will be locked and cannot be edited. Once your application is submitted, you will receive a confirmation at the top of the page and an email confirmation to your email address. Do I have to register an account? Yes, to start your application, you need to register an account in our recruitment system. Click on \"Log in\" or \"Register\" in our recruitment system . With an account, you will have an overview of your applications and can reuse information you have previously entered. Who gets access to the information I provide in my application? The information you provide will be accessible to HR and recruiting personnel within the organisation, such as HR managers or equivalents, recruiting managers, members of selection committees, and, where applicable, external experts or equivalents. The University of Gothenburg is a government agency, and your application documents constitute a public document according to the principle of public access to information. This means that the public has the right to access your application, attached documents, and correspondence with us. If you have a protected identity, please contact the contact person specified in the advertisement. Only provide information that is relevant to the specific position. Can I get notifications when there are new vacancies? You can subscribe to our vacancies via our recruitment system. When new positions become available, you will receive notifications to your email address. Step 2. Selection Once the application deadline has passed, we review all incoming applications. Then, we select a number of individuals for interviews based on the requirements specified in the advertisement. If you are chosen for an interview, we will contact you. At the University of Gothenburg, there are many different types of positions, so the recruitment process may vary depending on the type of position. What happens when I apply for a teaching post? The recruitment process for teaching positions follows the same principles as other types of positions, but the process looks a bit different and takes longer as it often involves opinions from external experts and preparation in a teacher proposal committee. Teaching positions, according to the employment regulations of the University of Gothenburg, include: professor university lecturer university adjunct assistant university lecturer adjunct professor guest professor adjunct university lecturer adjunct university adjunct guest lecturer postdoctoral researcher. Step 3. Offer and employment If you are offered the position, you will be contacted to discuss the terms of employment and the starting date. When you are employed by the University of Gothenburg, you will receive a certificate of employment by email. The document is digitally signed by the employer and does not require a signature from you as an employee. The certificate of employment corresponds to an employment contract and has the same legal validity. From January 2026 , this will apply to all new employments. Along with your certificate, you will also receive an employment appendix outlining the terms and conditions of your employment. In addition to your local workplace introduction, there is also a digital orientation course for newly hired employees where you will gain general knowledge about the University and what you need to be aware of. Welcome Services also offers information and assistance to international researchers, faculty, staff, and students in matters concerning the arrival to and their stay at the University of Gothenburg. Warm welcome to Gothenburg University! How do I know that I have been hired - I haven't signed anything? When you receive a certificate of employment from the University of Gothenburg, this means that you are employed. No signature is required from you – it is your manager’s signature that validates the employment. This applies to employments starting from January 2026. How do I receive my certificate of employment? The certificate of employment is sent to the email address you provided in connection with your employment. Who do I contact if I have questions? Contact your manager at the department or division where you will be working. When do I get my salary? The University’s salaries are set individually. Salaries are paid on the 25th of each month. If the 25th is a Saturday, salaries are paid on the 24th, and if the 25th is a Sunday, salaries are paid on the 26th. In June and December, salaries may be paid on other dates as well, due to Christmas and Midsummer. Salaries can never be paid in advance. Register your salary account To receive your salary from the university, you need to register your bank account with Swedbank. The easiest way is to log in using BankID, and you can register an account from any Swedish bank. If you don’t have BankID or wish to register a foreign account, you will need to visit a Swedbank branch in person and present valid identification. Taxes When you start your employment, you must submit information about your A-tax status for the current year, and any applicable tax adjustment decision, in the payroll system. If you do not do this, you risk having a higher preliminary tax deducted from your salary. Collective agreement and union representatives The terms and conditions of your employment are regulated by agreements between the Swedish Agency for Government Employers and the main trade unions SACO, OFR-S and SEKO-civil. An agreement titled Villkorsavtal/Villkorsavtal-T regulates the general employment conditions. The University of Gothenburg also has a local collective agreement in place, Villkorsavtal-GU, which specifies additions to and exceptions from the other agreements. The union representatives There are three main union organisations represented at the University of Gothenburg. OFR-S The Union of Civil Servants Visit address: Karl Gustavsgatan 12 B Postal address: Box 100, 405 30 Göteborg Phone: 031-7861169 E-mail: st@st.fack.gu.se The Swedish Teachers’ Union Visit address: Karl Gustavsgatan 12B Postal address: Box 100, 405 30 Göteborg Phone: 031-786 6029 E-mail: lararforbundet@gu.se Saco-S Saco-S council Visit address: Karl Gustavsgatan 12B Postal address: Box 100, 405 30 GÖTEBORG E-mail: saco@gu.se SULF Göteborgs universitet The Swedish Association of University Teachers and Researchers Visit address: Karl Gustavsgatan 12 B Postal address: Box 100, 405 30 Göteborg SEKO The Union for Service and Communication Employees Visit address: Erik Dahlbergsgatatan 11 B Postal address: Box 100, 405 30 Göteborg Phone: 031-786 64 56, 070-877 34 95 E-mail: salima.khamchane@gu.se The union representative for trade union Saco-S University Administration Maja Pelling maja.pelling@gu.se 031-786 1165 Ivar Armini ivar.armini@gu.se 031-786 6510 School of Business, Economics and Law Pia Lundahl pia.lundahl@gu.se 031-786 5574 Fredric Gunve fredric.gunve@gu.se Faculty of Humanities Anna Holgén anna.holgen@gu.se 031-786 4602 Håkan Kellgren hakan.kellgren@gu.se 031-786 49 35 Faculty of Fine, Applied and Performing Arts Emil Östlund emil.ostlund@gu.se Martin Nordeborg martin.nordeborg@sprak.gu.se 031-786 36 63 Faculty of Science and Technology Maria Ahlstedt maria.ahlstedt@gu.se 031-786 10 77 Ann Nordberg ann.nordberg@ped.gu.se Sahlgrenska Academy Klas Eriksson klas.eriksson@gu.se 031-786 1989 Maria Nordqvist maria.nordqvist@gu.se 031-786 51 60 Faculty of Social Sciences Auður Magnúsdóttir audur.magnusdottir@history.gu.se 031-786 4626 Klas Eriksson klas.eriksson@gu.se 031-786 1989 University Library Håkan Kellgren hakan.kellgren@gu.se 031-786 49 35 Emil Östlund emil.ostlund@gu.se Faculty of Education Martin Nordeborg Martin Nordeborg@sprak.gu.se 031-786 36 63 Linnéa Wallgren linnea.wallgren@bioenv.gu.se 031-786 2527 The union representative for the trade union SEKO Salima Khamchane salima.khamchane@gu.se 031-786 6456 The union representative for the trade union OFR-S You can always reach the trade union ST at the University of Gothenburg, and OFR-S at st@st.fack.gu.se Central University Administration and National Units Peter Brandt peter.brandt@gu.se Anna Nilsson anna.nilsson@socmed.gu.se Faculty of Education Peter Brandt (Fackförbundet ST) peter.brandt@gu.se Marcus Löfdahl (Sveriges Lärare) marcus.lofdahl@hsm.gu.se Faculty of Fine, Applied and Performing Arts Filip Radovic (Fackförbundet ST) filip.radovic@filosofi.gu.se Jörgen Berg (Sveriges Lärare) jorgen.berg@hsm.gu.se Faculty of Humanities Lars Malmsten lars.malmsten@gu.se Faculty of Science and Technology Madelen Hansson madelen.hansson@gs.gu.se Adam Andersson adam.fredrik.andersson@gu.se Faculty of Social Sciences Helena Rohdén helena.rohden@gu.se Sahlgrenska Academy Filip Radovic (Fackförbundet ST) filip.radovic@filosofi.gu.se Anita Österberg (Sveriges Lärare) anita.osterberg@gu.se School of Business, Economics and Law Solveig Persson solveig.persson@sprak.gu.se Adam Andersson adam.fredrik.andersson@gu.se University Library Solveig Persson solveig.persson@sprak.gu.se Daniel Hermansson daniel.hermansson@gu.se FAQ What are the different professional areas? You have the option to filter for professions you are looking for on the Vacancies page. We have divided our professions into different job categories. Doctoral student Under this area, you will find our doctoral positions as well as professions such as teaching assistants and clinical assistants. Technical-/ and Administrative Staff Under this area, you will find, among other roles, positions such as project managers, developers, communicators, or economists. Teaching staff Under this area, you will find, among other roles, professions such as professors, university lecturers, university adjuncts, and postdoctoral researchers. Researchers Under this area, you will find, among other roles, professions such as researchers and research assistants. Will I be informed if the position has been filled? When we have filled a position, we contact all applicants personally or via email, regardless of the type of position you have applied for. Employment decisions are also announced on the digital notice board located at the entrance of the Humanities Library, Renströmsgatan 4. Can I appeal the decision? If you wish to appeal the decision to the Higher Education Appeals Board (Överklagandenämnden för högskolan, ÖNH), you must do so in writing. In your appeal, you should specify which decision you are appealing and the change to the decision that you request. It is also important to provide reasons why this change should be made. Include your address, and preferably also your telephone number and email address, as well as the reference number stated on the decision. A decision may only be appealed by the person concerned. The letter should be addressed to the Higher Education Appeals Board and sent to: University of Gothenburg Registrar's Office Box 100 405 30 Gothenburg The appeal must reach the University of Gothenburg within three (3) weeks from the day the decision was posted on the University of Gothenburg's notice board. Please note that decisions regarding employment as a doctoral student cannot be appealed. Related content Vacancies Time for a change? Find vacancies at the University of Gothenburg. About the University Employment benefits There are many benefits to working at the University of Gothenburg. We offer various perks such as wellness grant, parental… Swedish Research Council Curious about conducting research in Sweden? External link Last modified 13 April 2026 Cookie information Use of cookies At gu.se, we use cookies to make the website function as well as possible. By clicking on \"Accept all cookies,\" you agree to our storing cookies. Certain features require so-called third-party cookies. These are required, among other things, for embedded video and audio clips from YouTube and SoundCloud to be playable. If you choose \"Accept necessary cookies,\" we will not activate third-party cookies. Read more about cookies. Necessary Marketing Accept all cookies Accept necessary cookies Contact The University of Gothenburg Box 100 405 30 Gothenburg Sweden Main Switchboard +46 31-786 00 00 Visiting address Find organisation Organisation identity number: 202100-3153 Our channels facebook linkedin youtube instagram Shortcuts Student portal (External link) Staff Portal (External link) University library (External link) Work at the University Press and media EUTOPIA About the website Processing personal data Cookie settings Accessibility report"
